WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:01.126
- [Voiceover] The first
thing I googled was

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:03.423
how to teach a guy without
arms to shoot a bow.

00:00:03.423 --> 00:00:05.101
And there's nothing out there like that.

00:00:05.101 --> 00:00:07.271
Because it's such a rare thing.

00:00:07.271 --> 00:00:09.813
(intense violin music)

00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:12.842
(bow shooting and striking)

00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:17.009
My name is Matt Stutzman,
I'm from Fairfield, Iowa.

00:00:17.848 --> 00:00:20.714
And I'm a professional archerer.

00:00:20.714 --> 00:00:23.088
- Well, that's how I shoot, there you go.

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:26.163
In 1982, I was born as you see me

00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:28.213
right now, without any arms.

00:00:28.213 --> 00:00:31.083
I never see not having
arms as a limitation.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:34.737
It's amazing how your body,
when it's missing something,

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:38.384
your other limbs take off and
kind of pick up the slack.

00:00:38.384 --> 00:00:40.188
So for me, my feet are my hands.

00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:42.931
Everything that I have in
my life, I do with my toes.

00:00:42.931 --> 00:00:46.168
It's pretty rare that I don't
use my feet for something.

00:00:46.168 --> 00:00:49.075
My phone, for example,
how I pick up my phone,

00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:51.252
I'd actually grab it
with my foot and flip it

00:00:51.252 --> 00:00:54.363
and catch it and be like hello.

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:57.434
When I got started shooting,
it took me about two weeks

00:00:57.434 --> 00:01:01.780
from looking at a bow till
shooting probably my first arrow.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.091
Because I had to figure out how to hold it

00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:06.084
with this toe or this toe
or this foot or that foot.

00:01:06.084 --> 00:01:09.036
I had to kinda think
outside the box and come up

00:01:09.036 --> 00:01:11.495
with some creative ways of shooting.

00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:13.745
I actually hold the bow with my right foot

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:17.721
but I will pretend it's
somebody's right arm in my mind.

00:01:17.721 --> 00:01:19.976
And then I have a release
aid that goes over my right

00:01:19.976 --> 00:01:22.927
shoulder and I actually
hook that onto the string.

00:01:22.927 --> 00:01:25.674
And when I sit up, I push
my foot away from my chest

00:01:25.674 --> 00:01:28.129
which draws the bow, at
this point, I'm aiming.

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:29.808
I don't see a guy without arms shooting.

00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:31.897
I see somebody with arms shooting

00:01:31.897 --> 00:01:33.659
and I guess it's just how I imagine it.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.012
(bow releasing and striking)

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:37.961
So I did repetitions, I sat in a chair

00:01:37.961 --> 00:01:41.317
for eight hours a day, six days a week.

00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:43.777
Time, kind of, slows way down.

00:01:43.777 --> 00:01:45.987
You forget who's around you, you forget

00:01:45.987 --> 00:01:48.118
what you're doing almost
and you're so focused

00:01:48.118 --> 00:01:52.585
on one thing, shot and shot
and shot and shot and shot.

00:01:52.585 --> 00:01:54.494
That’s all I did, this
bow right here probably

00:01:54.494 --> 00:01:56.667
has a million arrows shot through it.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.906
At the end of the day, ya
know, it helps you become good.

00:01:59.906 --> 00:02:03.020
A couple medals or trophies
that stand out to me

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.271
is my paralymics silver
medal, I also have the

00:02:05.271 --> 00:02:08.263
Guinness world record for the
longest accurate archery shot.

00:02:08.263 --> 00:02:12.430
And I shot an arrow and hit
a target from 310 yards away.

00:02:13.469 --> 00:02:15.804
I want my kids to see that no matter what

00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:17.689
the challenge is you can overcome it.

00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:20.352
You just have to put your
head down and push through

00:02:20.352 --> 00:02:22.606
and figure out a way to be successful.

00:02:22.606 --> 00:02:23.926
Figure out a way to just, ya know,

00:02:23.926 --> 00:02:26.218
be a good person while
you do all that stuff.

00:02:26.218 --> 00:02:27.056
At the end of the day I just want to be

00:02:27.056 --> 00:02:30.002
the best in the world, I
don't care if you have arms,

00:02:30.002 --> 00:02:31.844
you don't have arms, I
don't care if you were

00:02:31.844 --> 00:02:33.361
the Michael Jordan of the sport

00:02:33.361 --> 00:02:34.755
and you're an able-bodied archer.

00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:35.778
I just want to beat you 'cause I

00:02:35.778 --> 00:02:38.342
want to be known as the
best archer in the world.

00:02:38.342 --> 00:02:39.409
(arrow releasing and striking)

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:42.576
(upbeat techno music)

